//leaf node- node with no children
//root node- base node of the tree
//edge - connection between two nodes
//binary tree- tree in which each node has at most two children
//Parent node  - node that has children
//Child node - node that is a descendant of a parent node
//ancestor node - node that is a parent of a node up to the root
//descendant node - node that is a child of a node
//sibling nodes - nodes that share the same parent
//internal node - node that has at least one child 
//depth - number of edges from the root to a node
//level - number of edges from the root to a node and the root is at level 0
//height of a tree - number of edges on the longest path from the root to a leaf
//binary search tree - binary tree in which the left child is less than the parent and the right child is greater than the parent
//full binary tree - binary tree in which every node has either 0 or 2 children
//complete binary tree - binary tree in which every level, except possibly the last, is completely filled, and all nodes are as far left as possible
//perfect binary tree - binary tree in which all internal nodes have two children and all leaves are at the same level
//bst search - searching for a value in a binary search tree
//bst insert - inserting a value in a binary search tree
//bst delete - deleting a value in a binary search tree
//bst traversal - traversing a binary search tree in a specific order
